// Shared vocabulary of the stage-2 permission modules (10-17): the recipient classes
// the disclosure paragraphs of sections 6103(d)-(o) name, and the two generic case
// facts every "upon written request" paragraph reads. A recipient class is a status
// of the disclosure (who receives it, in which capacity); the purpose, content and
// extent limits of each paragraph are separate per-paragraph case facts declared next
// to the rule that reads them. Nothing here derives a conclusion: the exceptions
// conclude `disclosure_permitted` (module 01), which defeats the section 6103(a)
// prohibition.

use self::{
    Disclosure,
    Organ,
};

